 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "hotpoint SA2 oven not heatin on fan, grill ok. wat does SA2 mean??"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "First, 'SA2' is simply the model number for this specific Hotpoint cooker design; it doesn't indicate a fault code. Regarding your oven: when you select the fan function, does the inside light come on and do you hear the fan running? Also, was the clock flashing or set to an automatic mode (like a timer) before you tried to use it?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "light comes on yes. fan isnt spinning tho, just a low hum from the back. clock is set and in manual"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "The 'low hum' without spinning strongly suggests the fan motor is trying to turn but can't—likely because it has seized up or the fan blade is obstructed. Please switch off and unplug the oven (or isolate it at the fuse box) and let it cool down completely. Then, remove the back panel inside the oven cavity to inspect the fan blade. Check if it spins freely by hand or if it's rubbing against the rear wall. Let me know what you find."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok isolated it at the cooker switch. fan blade is very stiff by hand, feels gritty. wat now?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Because the fan cannot turn, it cannot circulate heat, which is why you get no warmth on the fan setting. Replacing an oven fan motor involves removing the rear panel inside the oven and disconnecting electrical wiring. This work requires isolating the appliance properly and handling internal components safely. I recommend calling a qualified engineer to replace the fan motor for you."
  }
 ],
